iew.googlesource.com/899777 Commit-Ready: Rajat Jain &lt;rajatja@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rajat Jain &lt;rajatja@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="899777" owner_email="rajatja@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/touch_updater" ref="refs/changes/77/899777/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib53e02d1e5c0f5b2d96d9a02fd33022f92e52b04" commit="b00f05700347027f3b2910d8208b98dad951d215" commit_message="Enable PD communication in RO for external display  This patch makes EC enable PD communication if it's running in manual recovery mode. This is required to show recovery screen on a type-c monitor.  This patch also makes EC-EFS ignore power availability. It will make EC verify &amp; jump to RW even if power is sourced by a barrel jack adapter. This should allow depthcharge to show screens (e.g. broken, warning) on a type-c monitor.  BUG=b:72387533 BRANCH=none TEST=On Fizz with type-c monitor, verify - Recovery screen is displayed in manual recovery mode. - Critical update screen is displayed in normal mode. - Warning screen is displayed in developer mode. Monitors tested: Dingdong, Dell S2718D  Change-Id: Ib53e02d1e5c0f5b2d96d9a02fd33022f92e52b04 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/898346 Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="898346" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/46/898346/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4901b27bbfedd54dc0d364b16c49d4ed0dea0fc4" commit="8d74e76f7d39b47558f9fa6ffda01183edffbdac" commit_message="Fizz: Suppress EC_CMD_PD_GET_LOG_ENTR debug log  Host command handler prints every single host command except when commands are repeated back-to-back. Some commands do not provide useful info when studying feedback reports or what is worse they may hide critical info by flooding the EC log.  BUG=chromium:803955 BRANCH=none TEST=Observe 'HC 0x115' is not printed.  Change-Id: I4901b27bbfedd54dc0d364b16c49d4ed0dea0fc4 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/896694 Reviewed-by: Vincent Palatin &lt;vpalatin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="896694" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/94/896694/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iedc34e29affacbea8daa2523306b252c3575d81b" commit="914c8082368a048fe110c8f4fb2db2b9d0f935dc" commit_message="Add new firmware_Bmpblk test to FAFT  This patch adds a new FAFT lv4 test to validate whether the firmware screen images have been correctly scaled for the device's panel resolution. In the past, we have repeatedly forgot to set this correctly in the bmpblk board.yaml, which means the respective Chromebooks shipped with images sized for 1366x768 that get scaled up at runtime and thus look very blurry. This test should finally prevent that from ever happening again.  The test itself merely checks for the existence of a flag file in the firmware image's CBFS. The &quot;heavy lifting&quot; is done by CL:898219 which makes the chromeos-bmpblk.ebuild insert this flag file into images whenever it runs with the fallback resolution.  BUG=None TEST=Ran on Kevin both with and without explicitly scaled images.  Change-Id: Iedc34e29affacbea8daa2523306b252c3575d81b Signed-off-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: ht